SINA_SMART["bacterio1-structure"] = {"lecture":"bacterio1-structure","title":"Bacterial structure, nutrition and metabolism","mapStatus":"auto: generated by universal.py from the lecture summary and key points; not human-reviewed","los":[{"id":"bacterio1-structure:s0","text":"Describe and explain: Bacteria in medicine","topic":"Bacteria in medicine","sec":0,"importance":"standard","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"bacterio1-structure:e0","text":"Prokaryotes: 0.2-5 µm, nucleoid, 70S ribosomes, no organelles, peptidoglycan.","topic":"Prokaryotic cell structure","sec":1,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"bacterio1-structure:e1","text":"Plasmids: small, non-essential, often resistance or virulence genes.","topic":"Prokaryotic cell structure","sec":1,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"bacterio1-structure:e2","text":"Capsule: anti-phagocytic, serotypes, vaccines (Hib, pneumococcus); slime: biofilm.","topic":"Prokaryotic cell structure","sec":1,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"bacterio1-structure:e3","text":"Gram+: thick peptidoglycan, teichoic acids; Gram-: thin PG + outer membrane with LPS.","topic":"Cell wall, membrane and appendages","sec":2,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"bacterio1-structure:e4","text":"β-lactams bind PBPs and block peptidoglycan synthesis.","topic":"Cell wall, membrane and appendages","sec":2,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"bacterio1-structure:e5","text":"Flagella (H antigen, motility); fimbriae (adhesion); sex pili (conjugation).","topic":"Cell wall, membrane and appendages","sec":2,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"bacterio1-structure:e6","text":"Endospores: Bacillus, Clostridium; resist heat and drying.","topic":"Cell wall, membrane and appendages","sec":2,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"bacterio1-structure:e7","text":"Most pathogens: mesophiles, neutral pH.","topic":"Growth requirements and culture media","sec":3,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"bacterio1-structure:e8","text":"Anaerobes lack SOD and catalase.","topic":"Growth requirements and culture media","sec":3,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"bacterio1-structure:e9","text":"Media: enriched (blood, chocolate), selective (MacConkey), differential, transport.","topic":"Growth requirements and culture media","sec":3,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"bacterio1-structure:e10","text":"Growth curve: lag, log, stationary, death; respiration vs fermentation.","topic":"Growth curve and metabolism","sec":4,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"}],"vmap":{},"mlevel":{"dl675r":"a","1n670u9":"a","3stmw6":"a","17j8vzg":"a","1c33r4s":"a","qaycua":"a","1cvgie0":"a","x0psco":"a","18sk5sh":"a","18nfet4":"a","nmvp00":"a","7o64tt":"a","g3b4xg":"a","gz5h7z":"a","181c4wp":"a"},"mapCounts":{"verified":0,"auto":15,"ambiguous":0,"missing":0},"mrules":[],"items":[],"experimental":[],"status":{},"difficulty":{},"expl":{"bacterio1-structure:s0":{"s":0,"u":["Microbiology studies microscopic organisms: bacteria, viruses, fungi and parasites.","Bacteria matter because their structure and physiology explain mechanisms of infection (adhesion, invasion, toxins, immune evasion), diagnosis , antibiotic choice and resistance , and prevention ."],"dp":[]},"bacterio1-structure:e0":{"s":1,"u":["Prokaryotes: 0.2-5 µm, nucleoid, 70S ribosomes, no organelles, peptidoglycan.","Prokaryotes are 0.2-5 µm , divide by binary fission , have no nuclear membrane (a nucleoid ), no membrane-bound organelles, 70S ribosomes (80S in eukaryotes), a single circular chromosome without histones, a membrane generally without sterols, and a peptidoglycan cell wall.","Components: external appendages (flagella, pili, fimbriae), glycocalyx (capsule, slime), envelope (outer membrane in Gram-negatives, peptidoglycan, cell membrane) and internal parts (cytoplasm, ribosomes, inclusions, nucleoid, sometimes endospores)."],"dp":[]},"bacterio1-structure:e1":{"s":1,"u":["Plasmids: small, non-essential, often resistance or virulence genes.","Genetic material : the chromosome carries essential genes; plasmids are small non-essential DNA molecules that may carry resistance or virulence genes."],"dp":[]},"bacterio1-structure:e2":{"s":1,"u":["Capsule: anti-phagocytic, serotypes, vaccines (Hib, pneumococcus); slime: biofilm.","Glycocalyx : a thick rigid capsule ( K. pneumoniae , Haemophilus , S. pneumoniae , B. anthracis ) protects from phagocytosis , defines serotypes (over 100 for pneumococcus) and is the basis of vaccines (Hib, pneumococcus); a thinner slime layer allows attachment and biofilm ( S. mutans )."],"dp":[]},"bacterio1-structure:e3":{"s":2,"u":["Gram+: thick peptidoglycan, teichoic acids; Gram-: thin PG + outer membrane with LPS.","Gram-positive walls have a thick peptidoglycan with teichoic and lipoteichoic acids; Gram-negative walls a thin peptidoglycan, a periplasmic space and an outer membrane with lipopolysaccharide (endotoxin) and porins."],"dp":[]},"bacterio1-structure:e4":{"s":2,"u":["β-lactams bind PBPs and block peptidoglycan synthesis.","Peptidoglycan is chains of N-acetylglucosamine and N-acetylmuramic acid cross-linked by peptides; β-lactams bind penicillin-binding proteins (PBPs), block its synthesis and the cell bursts from internal pressure."],"dp":[]},"bacterio1-structure:e5":{"s":2,"u":["Flagella (H antigen, motility); fimbriae (adhesion); sex pili (conjugation).","Pili : longer, few; sex (conjugation) pili transfer plasmids.","Fimbriae : short, numerous, for adhesion and biofilm."],"dp":[]},"bacterio1-structure:e6":{"s":2,"u":["Endospores: Bacillus, Clostridium; resist heat and drying.","Endospores ( Bacillus , Clostridium ) resist heat, drying and starvation and germinate when conditions improve."],"dp":[]},"bacterio1-structure:e7":{"s":3,"u":["Most pathogens: mesophiles, neutral pH.","Physical : temperature (psychrophiles, psychrotrophs that spoil refrigerated food such as Pseudomonas , mesophiles 10-47 °C including most pathogens, thermophiles, hyperthermophiles), pH (most at 6.5-7.5), water and osmotic pressure (halophiles need salt; osmotolerant bacteria such as staphylococci tolerate it)."],"dp":[]},"bacterio1-structure:e8":{"s":3,"u":["Anaerobes lack SOD and catalase.","Oxygen tolerance depends on superoxide dismutase and catalase/peroxidase , which strict anaerobes lack.","Chemical : oxygen : obligate aerobes ( Pseudomonas , Neisseria ), obligate anaerobes ( Clostridium , Bacteroides ), facultative anaerobes ( E. coli , staphylococci), aerotolerant anaerobes and microaerophiles ( Campylobacter )."],"dp":[]},"bacterio1-structure:e9":{"s":3,"u":["Media: enriched (blood, chocolate), selective (MacConkey), differential, transport.","By use: simple (nutrient agar), enriched (blood agar, chocolate agar), selective (MacConkey for Gram-negatives, mannitol salt for staphylococci), enrichment (selenite F for Salmonella ), differential (lactose on MacConkey, mannitol on Chapman, haemolysis on blood agar), transport (Cary-Blair, Amies).","Culture media are sterile (autoclave, 120 °C)."],"dp":[]},"bacterio1-structure:e10":{"s":4,"u":["Growth curve: lag, log, stationary, death; respiration vs fermentation.","In a closed culture the growth curve has four phases: lag (adaptation, no increase), exponential (log) (fastest division), stationary (division equals death) and death ."],"dp":[{"h":"Why the growth phase matters for antibiotics","t":"Many antibiotics, especially β-lactams, kill bacteria while they are building new wall, so they work best in the exponential phase. Bacteria in the stationary phase, or inside a biofilm where nutrients and oxygen are scarce, divide slowly and survive these drugs even without resistance genes ( tolerance ). That is why infections on catheters, prosthetic valves or joints relapse so often, and why they may need the device removed or long, combined treatment. Source: the lecture's growth curve, slime layer and β-lactam mode of action."}]}},"meta":{"dl675r":{"a":"recall","vg":"bacterio1-structure:e0/recall/1"},"1n670u9":{"a":"recall","vg":"bacterio1-structure:e0/recall/2"},"3stmw6":{"a":"recall","vg":"bacterio1-structure:e0/recall/3"},"17j8vzg":{"a":"recall","vg":"bacterio1-structure:e6/recall/1"},"1c33r4s":{"a":"recall","vg":"bacterio1-structure:e2/recall/1"},"qaycua":{"a":"recall","vg":"bacterio1-structure:e3/recall/1"},"1cvgie0":{"a":"recall","vg":"bacterio1-structure:e3/recall/2"},"x0psco":{"a":"recall","vg":"bacterio1-structure:e4/recall/1"},"18sk5sh":{"a":"recall","vg":"bacterio1-structure:e5/recall/1"},"18nfet4":{"a":"recall","vg":"bacterio1-structure:e6/recall/2"},"nmvp00":{"a":"recall","vg":"bacterio1-structure:e8/recall/1"},"7o64tt":{"a":"recall","vg":"bacterio1-structure:e9/recall/1"},"g3b4xg":{"a":"recall","vg":"bacterio1-structure:e9/recall/1"},"gz5h7z":{"a":"recall","vg":"bacterio1-structure:e9/recall/2"},"181c4wp":{"a":"recall","vg":"bacterio1-structure:e10/recall/1"}},"explRev":"abac2f8eebb1"};
